## 7. Breaking-change check between revisions
   concept: a consumer written against v1 must keep working: removing or retyping a response field, or adding a required parameter, breaks it; adding an operation, an optional field or a deprecation does not. CI runs this on every change to the spec
   $ npx tsx src/breaking.ts openapi/v1.yaml openapi/v2.yaml
   |    openapi/v1.yaml (1.0.0) -> openapi/v2.yaml (1.1.0)
   |      ok        GET /employers/{employerId}/members 200 body.items[].phone: added (tolerant readers ignore it)
   |      ok        GET /members/{memberId} 200 body.phone: added (tolerant readers ignore it)
   |      ok        GET /members/{memberId}/contributions: deprecated (still served until its Sunset date)
   |      ok        GET /contributions: operation added
   |    0 breaking, 4 compatible
   -> exit 0
   $ npx tsx src/breaking.ts openapi/v1.yaml openapi/v2-breaking.yaml
   |    openapi/v1.yaml (1.0.0) -> openapi/v2-breaking.yaml (2.0.0-draft)
   |      BREAKING  GET /employers/{employerId}/members 200 body.items[].joinedOn: removed from the response
   |      BREAKING  GET /members/{memberId} 200 body.joinedOn: removed from the response
   |      BREAKING  GET /members/{memberId}/contributions query.year: new required parameter
   |      BREAKING  GET /members/{memberId}/contributions 200 body.items[].memberAmount: type number -> string
   |      BREAKING  GET /members/{memberId}/contributions 200 body.items[].employerAmount: type number -> string
   |      ok        GET /employers/{employerId}/members 200 body.items[].startDate: added (tolerant readers ignore it)
   |      ok        GET /members/{memberId} 200 body.startDate: added (tolerant readers ignore it)
   |    5 breaking, 2 compatible
   -> exit 1

